                <pb facs="0442" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2333: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-27T19:00:00-05:00">October 27, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>119. Your 257, October 26, 1 p.m. You should continue maintaining contact with
                    Drummond and exchanging with him, under the same conditions as heretofore as to
                    confidence, such information on developments in and respecting the China-Japan
                    matter as may appear to be of significance.</p>
                <p>In the interim preceding the Council’s reconvening, it is suggested that unless
                    data information seems to be of peculiar significance or timeliness, it may be
                    forwarded by mail rather than by telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
